          "filename": "Lakshminarayan brick.jpg",
          "caption": "A Brick found in Bhismak Nagar fort with the inscription \"...Pati Shri Shri Pratyaksh Narayan Sri Lakshmi Narayan\". The copperplate grant of 1401 found in Ghilamora records the the Chutia king Lakshminarayan, son of Satynarayan, while the 1392 Dhenukhona copperplate records Pratyakshnarayan as a king who reissued Satyanarayan's previous grant. Both these may either be the same king or brothers as evident from this inscription. The words before Pati aren't readable. It probably formed a word like Sadhayapati.",
          "alt": "A Brick found in Bhismak Nagar fort with the inscription \"...Pati Shri Shri Pratyaksh Narayan Sri Lakshmi Narayan\". The copperplate grant of 1401 found in Ghilamora records the the Chutia king Lakshminarayan, son of Satynarayan, while the 1392 Dhenukhona copperplate records Pratyakshnarayan as a king who reissued Satyanarayan's previous grant. Both these may either be the same king or brothers as evident from this inscription. The words before Pati aren't readable. It probably formed a word like Sadhayapati.",
